# v2.0.0-beta.6 release hold

Status: BLOCKED_BY_EVIDENCE_PROVENANCE

Reason:
The real-pilot workspace currently verifies reviewer rows only at the authorized
Session/profile/Space cohort level. It does not yet bind every independent-review
row to the immutable event/prediction row frozen in independent-review.seed.jsonl,
and evaluate does not re-verify the seed hash before aggregation.

Without event-level binding, a synthetically added reviewer row for an authorized
Session could inflate Stable metric sample counts or scores.

Do not publish v2.0.0-beta.6 until:
1. review rows are fail-closed against the frozen seed event identity + immutable
   prediction/runtime provenance;
2. the frozen seed hash is revalidated during evaluate;
3. regressions prove invented events and modified predictions/origin are rejected;
4. the exact merged main SHA passes full CI;
5. this hold is removed in a separate final unhold change.
